+# Derive a missing post excerpt from the body
+
+## Context
+
+The excerpt is the teaser shown on the post cards at `/posts` and one of the
+two columns `posts.search` matches on, so it must never be empty. It used to
+be a required form field, but writers reported that they mostly pasted the
+opening of the body into it by hand.
+
+## Decision
+
+`excerpt` is optional on the create and edit forms. When it arrives missing,
+empty, or whitespace-only, the server writes one from the body — on create and
+on update alike, so an update that clears the field re-derives from the *new*
+body. A provided excerpt always wins and is stored trimmed, as before.
+
+The rule lives in [app/Support/excerpt.ts](../../app/Support/excerpt.ts) and
+runs against the trimmed body:
+
+- 140 characters or fewer: the whole body, no ellipsis.
+- Otherwise the first 140 characters, cut back to the last whitespace when
+  character 141 would split a word (both character 140 and 141 non-whitespace);
+  a run of 140 characters with no whitespace is cut at 140.
+- The kept part is right-trimmed and closed with a single `…` (U+2026).
+
+Title and body stay required — a blank one is still a 422 and saves nothing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The stored excerpt is still never empty, so the cards, the post page, and
+search need no fallback of their own. The derivation is a plain function, so it
+is unit-tested without a database (`tests/excerpt.test.ts`), and both
+controller paths call it through `resolveExcerpt()` rather than repeating the
+"blank means derive" check.
